. ForkJoinPool Internals (Deep Dive)
Parallel streams are powered by the ForkJoinPool, introduced in Java 7.
Divide and Conquer

Split task recursively
Execute in parallel
Merge results

Work-Stealing Algorithm (Most Important)
 Its own deque (double-ended queue)
Threads pushes the task in their own queue
excecute the task from LIFO

When thread becomes idle
It steal task from bottom FIFO of another thread

Why this works:
✔ reduces contention
✔ improves CPU utilization
✔ balances load automatically

